  "finalText": "All done. Here's what was implemented across the three layers:\n\n### Changes\n\n**1. Core port** (`packages/core/src/ports/benchmark.port.ts`):\n- Added `\"cancelled\"` to `SuiteStatus` type (line 156) — previously only `\"created\" | \"running\" | \"completed\" | \"failed\"`\n- Added `BenchmarkCancelResult` interface and `cancelSuite()` to `BenchmarkPort` (already existed in the port but wasn't wired)\n\n**2. Job/Process layer** (`apps/server/src/jobs.ts`):\n- Wired `JobStore` (the pre-existing JSON-backed store) into `JobManager` via `persist()` calls at all status transitions: create → running → terminal state, and on `cancel()` — so job cancellation is durably persisted to `.codeatlas/benchmarks/jobs/<id>.json`\n\n**3. API/Store layer** (`apps/server/src/routes.ts`):\n- `POST /benchmarks/:id/cancel`: now calls `store.updateSuiteStatus(suiteId, \"cancelled\")` to durably mark the suite on disk\n- `POST /jobs/:id/cancel`: same — persists suite status when the job has a `suiteId`\n- `startBenchmarkJob` finally block: now calls `store.updateSuiteStatus()` alongside `markSuiteInterrupted()` when a job is cancelled\n\n**4. Tests** (82 tests pass across 9 files):\n- `packages/benchmark/tests/store.test.ts`: added test for `updateSuiteStatus(\"cancelled\")`\n- `packages/benchmark/tests/cancel.test.ts`: fixed pre-existing missing `Result` import\n- `apps/server/tests/api.test.ts`: updated 3 cancellation tests to verify suite status on disk:\n  - **Cancelled queued job**: verifies job status is `\"cancelled\"`, stages are all cancelled\n  - **Cancelled in-flight job**: verifies job status is `\"cancelled\"`, suite.json on disk has `status: \"cancelled\"`, and `repository.json` has `interruptedAt`\n  - **Already-finished job**: returns 409, job stays `\"completed\"`, suite.json stays `\"completed\"` — no state corruption",
